{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a multimodal fusion approach (combining RNA and image modalities) provides a meaningful accuracy advantage over single-modality baselines, and what a reasonable multimodal baseline achieves. config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) represents a well-motivated 'standard' multimodal setup: a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) captures cell-type structure, resnet50 provides a robust image representation, avgpool is a low-risk aggregation, and weighted fusion is a common, stable combination strategy. Testing this first establishes a reference accuracy from which all subsequent experiments (stronger encoders, transformer aggregation, alternative fusion, single-modality baselines) can be interpreted. If it performs well, we exploit by upgrading components; if it underperforms, we learn that multimodal fusion at this complexity level is insufficient and pivot toward single-modality or more expressive architectures. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the 10-experiment budget."
}

